    "-": "",
    "1. Get a ROM: Official ROMs downloads one for your phone.  2. Verify ROM checks it's complete.  3. Convert to full ROM makes an image folder (to flash from OPxFlasher) or a recovery zip.  Then flash it on the Flash ROM tab.": "",
    "1. Your root app": "",
    "2. Stock image of the build the phone is running now": "",
    "3. Patch it on the phone": "",
    "4. Flash (current slot only)": "",
    "A Critical or Full backup made by OPxFlasher": "",
    "A backup lets you go back if something goes wrong. Without one, the ROM can still be flashed again. Every other safety check stays on.": "",
    "AERA, OrangeFox or TWRP stays installed. Not possible when part of the flash runs in fastbootd (it starts from the recovery partition): then the ROM's recovery is written and you're told so.": "",
    "AERA, OrangeFox or TWRP stays on the phone after flashing the zip.": "",
    "AERA: AERA's own image-zip install (it checks the model and anti-rollback).\nOrangeFox / TWRP: a normal flashable zip. It checks this is the same phone, the same slot and unchanged bootloader firmware, verifies every file, then restores.": "",
    "AIO tool for OnePlus / OPPO devices: backup, check, flash, restore and rescue.": "",
